      "Credential exposure: printing, copying, or sending tokens and keys (`gh auth token`, `gcloud auth print-*-token`, `op item get --reveal`, `op` listing, `rclone config show`, `fly`/`wrangler` token commands), or reading a credential store to get around a failed authentication",
      "Irreversible remote deletion: deleting a repository by any route (`gh repo delete`, REST, GraphQL); deleting remote refs (`push --delete`, `push origin :ref`, `DELETE …/git/refs`) and mirror pushes",
      "Unrecoverable local deletion: recursive `rm` in any flag order (`rip` is the recoverable path), `rip -d`, and disk-overwriting `dd`/`mkfs`",
      "Raw publication: registry publishing in any form (`npm`, `pnpm -r`, `cargo`, `uv`, `deno`, `bun`, `twine`, `gem`, `docker push`), unpublish/yank/dist-tag, `gh release` mutations, and `gh skill publish`; releases run only through the reviewed project release task",
      "Guardrail bypass: signing commits with `-S`/`--gpg-sign`; Worktrunk `--no-hooks`/`--yes`/force flags and forced branch or worktree deletion; vault registration and default-vault changes"
    ]
